# Better Auth (Indie Kit)

Full migration workflow: Cursor command **`migrate-to-better-auth`** (`.cursor/commands/migrate-to-better-auth.md`).

## Server session

```typescript
import { auth, type AuthSession } from "@/auth";

const session = await auth.api.getSession({ headers: req.headers });
// or in RSC: headers: await headers()
```

## Client

```typescript
import { authClient } from "@/lib/auth-client";
// signIn.social | signIn.email | signIn.magicLink | signUp.email | signOut
```

Never `useSession` from `next-auth/react`. Use `useUser()` for profile data.

## Drizzle adapter (critical)

`user.modelName` is `"app_user"` → schema key must be `app_user: users`, not `user: users`.

## Redirects

Use `redirectToSignIn(buildCallbackUrl(path, searchParams))` — not bare `redirect("/sign-in")`.

## Env

- `BETTER_AUTH_URL`, `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` (not `NEXTAUTH_*`)

## Existing DB upgrade

```bash
psql "$DATABASE_URL" -f drizzle/upgrades/0000_backfill_app_user.sql
psql "$DATABASE_URL" -f drizzle/upgrades/0001_better_auth_migration.sql
pnpm db:migrate
```

Fresh DB: `pnpm db:migrate` only.

## Admin plugin — roles & custom permissions

Docs: https://better-auth.com/docs/plugins/admin#roles

Default (no custom AC): `app_user.role` is `admin` or `user`. Super-admin routes use `withSuperAdminAuthRequired`.

### Custom permissions (forks / advanced)

1. Define statement + access controller in e.g. `src/auth/permissions.ts`:

```typescript
import { createAccessControl } from "better-auth/plugins/access";
import { defaultStatements, adminAc } from "better-auth/plugins/admin/access";

export const statement = {
  ...defaultStatements,
  project: ["create", "update", "delete"],
} as const;

export const ac = createAccessControl(statement);

export const user = ac.newRole({ project: ["create"] });
export const admin = ac.newRole({ project: ["create", "update"], ...adminAc.statements });
```

2. Pass to **both** server and client plugins:

```typescript
admin({ ac, roles: { admin, user, myCustomRole } })
adminClient({ ac, roles: { admin, user, myCustomRole } })
```

3. Check permissions — do not hand-roll role checks for admin features:

```typescript
await auth.api.userHasPermission({
  body: { userId, permission: { project: ["create"] } },
});
```

4. **`adminRoles`**: only when **not** using custom AC. With custom AC, permissions come from `ac` + `roles`.

5. Multiple roles on one user: comma-separated in `app_user.role`.

## Organization ACL (B2B Kit only)

B2B uses `src/auth/org-permissions.ts` with Better Auth organization plugin. See b2b-kit `.cursor/rules/better-auth.mdc` for `orgPerm` bundles and membership-only vs permission-gated routes.

## Do not add

- Custom NextAuth routes or `Session` types
- `bcryptjs` / custom password helpers
- Legacy signup/reset API routes (Better Auth handles natively)
- Custom zod enums mirroring Better Auth default admin/user roles
